For the cell 'an object holding a literal true / nothing around it', I use the kernel `conformance.kernel.recovery`. The rule for this kernel states that it returns 'The object the harness recovers from the reply, as canonical JSON, or NO_OBJECT' [65ae18af7a738b26]. For an input consisting of the object `{"z": true}` with nothing around it, the harness recovers this object. Replacing it with the well-formed object `{"z": 0}` changes the recovered object from `{"z": true}` to `{"z": 0}`. Therefore, the answer moves.